{% macro cause_hypotheses(causes, heading) -%}
{# Session R2-BUILD. Rendered ONLY when a bearing fault was committed AND the
   approved cause library returned entries for it -- report/generate.py's
   cause_section() returns None otherwise and this whole block disappears.
   Every string below comes from knowledge/causes.yaml through
   knowledge/loader.lookup_causes(); this macro selects and prints, it never
   derives, ranks or rewords. Both the deterministic report and the drafted
   report import this same macro, so the block is byte-identical on both paths
   by construction -- the Session R1 damage_stage precedent, applied again. #}
{% if causes %}
## {{ heading }}

**These are hypotheses, not findings.** The analysis committed
{{ causes.fault_labels | join(" and ") }} from the measured spectrum. What follows is the
reference library's list of causes known to produce that fault, in its own
order — **none of them is confirmed by this measurement, and this
analysis did not perform the inspection that would settle any of them.** A
vibration reading identifies the fault; it does not identify what caused it.
Each entry below names the evidence that would confirm or exclude it, split by
who can collect it.

_"Checked by this analysis" means the pipeline assessed evidence of that kind in
the reading it was given — not that a measurement was taken specifically to test
that cause. Bracketed references resolve against `references/INDEX.md`.
`(our reasoning)` marks an observation that is ours rather than something a
cited source states._
{% for cause in causes.causes %}

### {{ cause.name }}

{{ cause.mechanism }} {{ cause.citations }}
{% if cause.consider %}

_{{ cause.consider }}_
{% endif %}
{% if cause.checked %}

**Checked by this analysis** — {{ "vibration and reading-history evidence" if causes.history_checked else "vibration evidence" }} the pipeline evaluated:
{% for item in cause.checked %}
- {{ item.text }} {{ item.citation }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if cause.collect %}

**Evidence to collect** — analyst fieldwork; not performed by this analysis:
{% for item in cause.collect %}
- {{ item.text }} _How to collect: {{ item.how }}_ {{ item.citation }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

